/Title (Description  The pivot divides the array into two nearly equal halves at every recursive step. On average, the pivot creates reasonably balanced partitions, resulting in  efficient sorting.  The pivot is always the smallest or largest element, creating highly unbalanced  partitions \(e.g., an already sorted array with a poor pivot choice\).)
